  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Structs stored as the columns of their members, nested and nullable, queried by path. Links load on first use: a [Link] is a get-only LinkCollection<T> (breaking: was an ICollection<T>), loaded with LoadAsync or await foreach, throwing LinkNotLoadedException while not loaded; LdbContext.LoadAsync(entities, e => e.Link, ct) loads one link of many entities in one read (breaking: replaces LoadAsync(entity, name, ct)). Many-to-many links through a generated join table ([LinkMany]). WhereLinkedAsync finds entities by what their links hold. Upsert, UpdateWhereAsync and DeleteWhereAsync write without reading first. VersionOf and AttachAsync carry a row version across requests, as an ETag and If-Match. WriteBlobAsync and OpenBlob read and write BlobRef content. A context opens at a ReadMode. A failed save leaves the context as it was, so it can be tried again. Entities without a key; [NewGuid] keys; FindAsync only compiles for an entity with a key. Fixes: a child moved between parents' links is moved, not deleted; links of an entity inserted in a save are followed by later saves; a graph of new entities is saved to its leaves; a foreign key set on a child wins over a link that still holds it. Build errors LDB1001 to LDB1013. Databases declared in code (breaking): an [LdbDatabase] class holds its entities and the static TableSchema properties it declares; the generator makes it an EntityDatabase<TDb> with OpenAsync, Model, EnsureTablesAsync (or MigrateAsync with Axiom.LDB.Migration) and OpenContextAsync, which returns an LdbContext<TDb>. A context opens only when the database's tables are exactly the model's, and lists every one that is not in TableMismatchException; Set<T> of another database's entity does not compile. LdbContext.OpenAsync, ValidateAsync and EnsureTableAsync<T> are gone. Migrations: the generator writes the bases of migration classes and each database's chain when Axiom.LDB.Migration is referenced; the package brings LdbMigrationAdd (dotnet build -t:LdbMigrationAdd -p:LdbMigration=Name -p:LdbDatabase=Db) and LdbStrictMigrations.",
